# Free models a default `dispatch.sh opencode` task (and every clawock-patrol round) tries, in
# order. The first line is the primary; the rest are the fallback pool the runner rotates through
# (after the last one it wraps back to the first). The pool is read at dispatch time, so edits
# apply without restarting the patrol service.
#
# Every entry must be in the Zen catalog (`opencode models opencode`) and cost nothing. The runner
# allows 2 attempts per pool line, so a dead entry is two wasted attempts per failing round.
#
# 2026-10-07 reorder, from the patrol run logs of 10-05..10-07 (242 attempts) and opencode.log.
# What decides the order is how a model behaves while the free tier throttles it (HTTP 429
# FreeUsageLimitError, "Rate limit exceeded"), because the limit is not always account-wide:
#   * longcat-2.5-preview-free and nemotron-3-ultra-free surface the 429 and the attempt ends in
#     about 80s (0 stalls in 65 attempts). They go first: a throttled try is cheap.
#   * space-bunny-free, mimo-v2.6-flash-free, muse-spark-1.3-contributor-free and
#     ling-3.0-flash-fin-free retry the 429 silently, so a throttled attempt burns the runner's
#     full 300s stall timer. On 10-07 five rounds were finished by nemotron-3-ultra-free as attempt
#     5, each after about 20 minutes spent waiting out the three stalling models ahead of it.
#     space-bunny-free was the primary and went from 21/24 first attempts (10-05) to 1/24 (10-07).
#   * exo-free, fledge-alpha-free (both 1M context) and ling-3.1-flash-free are new in the catalog
#     (2026-09-29..10-06), declare tool calling, and answered 429 on 10-07 like everything else,
#     so they are alive but have not finished a round here yet. They sit last, where they are
#     reached only after every proven model failed.
#   * removed: mimo-v2.5-free and union-alpha. Both are out of the catalog and answer "Unexpected
#     server error" (13/13 attempts each on 10-07).
#   * left out on purpose: big-pickle (2025 stealth, 200k context) and nemotron-3.5-lightning-free
#     (small fast tier) — kcn wants good models first. opencode-go is not an option: the key in
#     ~/.local/share/opencode/auth.json has no active subscription.
#
# Some windows throttle every model at once (10-07 00:50-06:30 and 16:48 onward); no order helps
# there. Re-probe before trusting this file: /root/tools/agent-dispatch/probe-free-models.sh --tool
opencode/longcat-2.5-preview-free
opencode/nemotron-3-ultra-free
opencode/space-bunny-free
opencode/mimo-v2.6-flash-free
opencode/muse-spark-1.3-contributor-free
opencode/ling-3.0-flash-fin-free
opencode/exo-free
opencode/fledge-alpha-free
opencode/ling-3.1-flash-free
